    "chunk_text": "resonance imaging. Pre-processing \u2013 Before a computer vision method can be applied to image data in order to extract some specific piece of information, it is usually necessary to process the data in order to ensure that it satisfies certain assumptions implied by the method. Examples are: Re-sampling to ensure that the image coordinate system is correct. Noise reduction to ensure that sensor noise does not introduce false information. Contrast enhancement to ensure that relevant information can be detected. Scale space representation to enhance image structures at locally appropriate scales. Feature extraction \u2013 Image features at various levels of complexity are extracted from the image data. Typical examples of such features are: Lines,",
